From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:14:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3399: a test option, the LPDDR4 left at its 400
 MHz training rate

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

NOVA_RK3399_DDR_400 (off) ends TPL's LPDDR4 init after the 400 MHz
training, before the switch to the final rate: a RAM boot over USB with
it tells the training apart from the rate switch.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig     | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig b/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig
index 8891db7d..04fd7cf6 100644
--- a/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig
+++ b/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig
@@ -85,6 +85,14 @@ config NOVA_RK3399_DDR_856
 	  so every timing is 6.5 % shorter in time than that set was made
 	  for: an option for a test boot from RAM over USB, not a default.
 
+config NOVA_RK3399_DDR_400
+	bool "LPDDR4 left at its 400 MHz training rate (a test)"
+	depends on NOVA_RK3399_MAINLINE && RAM_ROCKCHIP_LPDDR4 && !NOVA_RK3399_DDR_856
+	help
+	  TPL trains the LPDDR4 at 400 MHz and stops there, with no switch
+	  to the final rate: for a RAM boot over USB that finds whether the
+	  training or the switch is what fails.
+
 config NOVA_RK3399_LADDER
 	def_bool NOVA_RK3399_CHAINLOAD || NOVA_RK3399_MAINLINE
 	help
diff --git a/drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c b/drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c
index 9e908965..ead7f73e 100644
--- a/drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c
+++ b/drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c
@@ -3024,6 +3024,10 @@ static int sdram_init(struct dram_info *dram,
 	if (params->base.dramtype == LPDDR4)
 		dfs_cfgs_lpddr4[1].base.ddr_freq = 856 * MHz;
 #endif
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NOVA_RK3399_DDR_400)) {
+		/* a test: stay at the 400 MHz the LPDDR4 is trained at */
+		return 0;
+	}
 	ret = dram->ops->set_rate_index(dram, params, 1);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
